<note version="0.3" xmlns:link="http://beatniksoftware.com/tomboy/link" xmlns:size="http://beatniksoftware.com/tomboy/size" xmlns="http://beatniksoftware.com/tomboy">
  <title>design principles</title>
  
<text xml:space="preserve"><note-content version="0.1"><underline>design principles</underline>

Desktop Principles
Typography
Numbers communicate information.
Units support numbers.
Never use pure black or pure white for text.
Material
Transparency exists to preserve context.
Blur exists only behind material.
Borders define material; opacity defines weight.
Interaction
Hover should acknowledge the pointer.
Active should feel stable, not loud.
Color communicates state, never decoration.
Composition
The wallpaper is part of the interface.
Persistent UI should almost disappear.
Temporary UI may carry the accent color.
Behavior
Every daemon must justify its existence.
Prefer composition over integration.
Prefer text files over opaque configuration.
</note-content></text>
